: [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le03ob10re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Write a response to the article.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le03ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le03ob10re2img07.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le03ob10re2img07.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn9le03ob10re2img07.jpg", "text": "Your ability to communicate through the written word will sometimes be more important than how you are able to communicate in person. When you write, no one will be able to see you to interpret your body language. They will not hear your tone of voice. This means that word choice is paramount.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn9le03ob10re2img05.jpg", "text": "It's a mistake to think, especially in the business world, that it's possible to be casual and not worry about grammatical structure when sending e-mails. Sending a business e-mail is like sending a letter or communicating in person. Of course it's true that we are more casual when sending e-mails to friends or family. However, when you are sending an e-mail to a business colleague, it is necessary to address the recipient in the same tone as you would when you speak to them in person. You must always keep in mind that the e-mail you send will be seen as a sample of how you communicate. Employers are certainly going to take note if they receive something written inappropriately. Even though we generally consider e-mails to be a quick, convenient way of communicating, it is still important to make sure you use proper grammar throughout. Employers are always keeping an eye out for those who communicate effectively and affect a professional presence. They take note when they see how well an employee can represent their company. Remember e-mails get forwarded. Abandon familiar texting abbreviations. Make sure that your words are formal and professional. Be as positive and respectful as you would if you were meeting the person face to face. Carefully review your e-mail before you send it and make any necessary revisions. That way, you will catch those small grammatical errors, incorrect punctuation, and find misspelled words.", "id": 2, "time": "19000"}, {"image": "engenn9le03ob10re2img06.jpg", "text": "Sending a thank you note is another way to present yourself as professional. Taking the time to thank someone when they help you makes it more more likely that they will refer you on to another person who may prove to be helpful to you. By showing your appreciation you will be more likely to be able to call on them again in the future.", "id": 3, "time": "115200"}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The World of Work", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Making a Difference", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe jobs and careers in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future with Will, Going to, The Present Continuous and The Simple Present", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We will reply back within a week.<br> I will forward you the e-mail.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm going to forward you the e-mail.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm forwarding all necessary attachments to you today.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I empty my inbox every morning.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Communication Etiquette in the Workplace", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A common way of communicating in the workplace is through e-mail. Here are some important tips to keep in mind when sending e-mails.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Don't forget to fill in the subject line in the \u201cSubject\u201d field.</li><li> Start the e-mail with a formal salutation like <span class=\"italic\">Hello Mr. ... </span>, <span class=\"italic\">Dear Ms. ... </span>, <span class=\"italic\">Dr. ...</span> </li><li> Type in the recipient's name properly like Jane B. Doe. Do not use either all lowercase or all uppercase letters.</li><li> Make sure that you have actually attached any files that you have mentioned.</li><li> Use proper sentence structure. Check for typing errors, proper punctuation and any grammatical errors before you send your e-mail.</li><li> Respond in a timely fashion.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "body language ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "changes in your body position and movements that show what you are feeling or thinking ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When you write, no one will be able to see you to interpret your body language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you may see in an article about professional etiquette.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tone of voice ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way your voice sounds, which shows how you are feeling or what you mean ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They will not hear your tone of voice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "word choice ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the use of words to convey meaning ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This means that word choice is paramount.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "recipient  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who receives something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Address the recipient of the e-mail in the same tone as you would when you speak to them in person.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sample", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a short written piece that demonstrates your ability to communicate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The e-mail you send will be seen as a sample of how you communicate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "professional presence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a mix of poise, self-confidence, control, and style that helps you project confidence  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Employers are always keeping an eye out for those who communicate effectively and affect a professional presence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le03ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Read the article from this lesson again.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Highlight the different tips that are included in the article.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you agree or disagree with these tips? Write down your answers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Will you use any of these tips in the future? Why or why not? Write down your answers. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Using all your answers. Write a short response (150-200 words) about the article. Read your response aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a response to professional information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I support my opinions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about my future plans.", "type": "text"}]}]}